* ============================================================
* Temperature sweep: `.DC TEMP -40 125 25` (Xyce: the sweep variable may
* be TEMP, in Celsius).
* The divider is a copper resistor model (TC1 = 0.0039 /K, TNOM = 27 C),
* so every point has a closed-form answer:
*     R(T)  = 1k * (1 + 0.0039*(T - 27))
*     Vout  = 10 * R(T) / (R(T) + 1k)
* ============================================================

.MODEL RCU R (R=1 TC1=0.0039 TNOM=27)

V1 in 0 DC 10
RT in out RCU 1k
RL out 0 1k

.DC TEMP -40 125 25

.END